From: Eduardo Garcia-Madico Portabella <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 23:19:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7325-nothing-spacewar: describe the
 PM8350B haptics

The vibration motor is an LRA on the haptics block of the PM8350B at 0xf000
(configuration) and 0xf100 (pattern), with the fifo-empty interrupt on
peripheral 0xf0, as in the vendor device tree. Resonance period 5880 us
(170 Hz). Peak drive voltage 1.8 V, the rated value for its 1.27 V RMS,
instead of the vendor 9.15 V overdrive.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts  | 18 ++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 18 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
index d5edc3c20..f87710062 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7325-nothing-spacewar.dts
@@ -2026,3 +2026,21 @@ &wifi {
 
 	status = "okay";
 };
+
+/*
+ * Vibration motor: an LRA driven by the haptics block of the PM8350B (vendor
+ * DT: qcom,hv-haptics@f000, reg 0xf000/0xf100/0xf200, fifo-empty interrupt,
+ * qcom,lra-period-us 5880, Vrms 1270 mV). Peak drive starts at 1.8 V, the
+ * motor's rated sqrt(2) x 1.27 V: the vendor 9.15 V vmax is overdrive for
+ * short pulses only.
+ */
+&pm8350b {
+	pm8350b_haptics: haptics@f000 {
+		compatible = "qcom,spmi-haptics";
+		reg = <0xf000>, <0xf100>;
+		interrupts = <0x3 0xf0 0x1 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+		interrupt-names = "fifo-empty";
+		qcom,vmax-microvolt = <1800000>;
+		qcom,lra-period-us = <5880>;
+	};
+};
